Add at max-width 900:
```
.hangar-side { order:2; width:100%; min-width:0; }
.dragon-list { flex-direction: row; ... width:100%; }
.hangar-side > .btn { width: 100%; flex: none; }
```
The width:100% won't fix if the parent grid track expands to content min-width. Set `.hangar-layout { min-width: 0; }` and `.hangar-side { min-width:0; overflow:hidden; }`? The grid item's min-width auto expands to content; setting min-width:0 and width:100% fixes. The `.dragon-list` flex row with overflow-x:auto will then be constrained by parent width. Add `min-width:0` to `.dragon-list` and `.hangar-side`. Also `.hangar-layout > * { min-width:0; }`.

Simplest:
```
@media(max-width:900px){
 .hangar-side { order:2; width:100%; min-width:0; }
 .dragon-list { width:100%; min-width:0; }
 .hangar-side > .btn { width:100%; }
}
```
The button width 100% will fix the 3009 width even if parent is wide? If parent width is 3009, 100% is 3009. But with min-width:0 and grid track 1fr, the parent should be 362. The grid container width is 362; grid track 1fr; item width auto; min-width auto based on content (3009). Setting min-width:0 lets it shrink to track. Add.

Also `.hangar-side` sets `width:100%`.

Now the "Explore the market" button will show.

Next, hangar empty vertical space: reduce hangar-center height from 34vh to 30vh and add a background gradient? With 30vh, the roster moves up 34px; the dragon may overlap the header? The dragon is below. It's okay.

The top empty area is 200-380. The dragon starts at 380. If we reduce the stage height, the roster moves up but the 3D dragon doesn't move. The dragon would overlap the roster. Not good.

Better: adjust the camera to make the dragon appear higher. In `showHangar`, cameraPos (13,6.8,17.5), target (0,3.4,0), FOV 50. The dragon at (0,2.6) appears near screen center (422) because target is 3.4. If we want it at ~320, look at a target below the dragon (e.g., y=0) -> the dragon appears above center. Let's estimate: target y 3.4, camera y 6.8, distance ~22; vertical FOV 50, screen 844. Angle to dragon center ~ (2.6-6.8)/22 = -0.19 rad vs target -0.155 rad, difference -0.035 rad -> ~-27px (below center). To move it up 100px, need +0.14 rad difference: target y such that angle = -0.19 - 0.14 = -0.33 => target y = 6.8 - tan(0.33)*22 = 6.8-7.6 = -0.8. That's below the platform. So target y ~ -0.5. Then the dragon appears 100px above center (~320), and the platform horizon would also move up. The dragon would be fully in the stage (180-467), and the empty sky below? The platform would be at ~350, filling below. That might look good: dragon centered in the stage, platform below.

But the camera target at y=-0.5 below ground, the view tilts down, showing more ground and less sky. The dragon at 320, platform horizon at ~430? Hard.

Let's try camera target y=1.0 (from 3.4) and camera position y=7.2. That raises the dragon by ~60px. And maybe reduce stage height to 32vh. We can iterate with a screenshot.

Also add a contact shadow blob under the dragon in the hangar (makePlayerModel has blob for rider, but hangar call doesn't pass blob; we removed the opts line so blob is always added for rider now! Wait we changed `if (rider)` so every player model with a rider gets a blob sprite. In hangar, rider true => blob under dragon. Is it visible? The blob is a dark sprite at y=-2.8 with scale 5x2.2 at the model origin; maybe hidden by the platform. It might appear as a shadow. Good.

But the blob's position is relative to the model group, scale 1.7 => 8.5x3.7, y=-4.76. The platform top at y=-4.6 (world). So the blob sits on the platform. Great, there should be a soft shadow. In the screenshot, under the dragon there is a green line/shadow? maybe.

Let's fix the width bug first, then adjust hangar camera framing.

Also the "Explore the market" button below the roster currently appears as an empty bar. Fix now.

